      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Secret Management**\n\nOkay, I'm thinking about how to build this Python file. I'm focusing on secret management. I'm leaning toward using AWS Secrets Manager as the provider; it's a solid choice for a number of reasons. Now, I have to figure out the best way to incorporate it into the code.\n\n\n**Defining Secret Retrieval**\n\nI've decided on AWS Secrets Manager as the external provider. Now, the implementation phase is starting to crystallize. I'll use `boto3` to interact with the `aws_secretsmanager` service. The goal is a `get_secret` function that takes the secret name, retrieving the value. This will be the heart of `fetch_db_secret.py`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818149524,
          "start": 1789818145985
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9798cc1001zdbIodQwzdfQnY",
